{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:51:35.664394Z","id":"1a16c82e06311cede52747c880ff16393a3a378bddc8ddb68022bfd0b5059710","body":{"detail":"Under wrangler 4.149.0 (workerd 1.20261006.1, the newest wrangler at least two weeks old on 2026-10-21) a dynamic Worker running `for(;;){}` with `limits: {cpuMs: 100}` held the whole runtime: no request to the parent Worker was answered for 30 s, until wrangler was stopped. 5000 arrays of 10000 numbers (about 200 MB) allocated without error, past the 128 MB the platform documents. test-sandbox.mjs therefore lists PLATFORM_ONLY's cases and runs none of them; that `cpuMs` ends each of them with CpuLimit, and the 128 MB isolate limit ends the two allocation cases with MemoryLimit, is unverified until they run on a deployed Worker.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":98},"end":{"line":128},"content_hash":"2ee8e634dcf7e40aee4418080aa0857b567a85c2b7bc8448dd1e9b600ac7460a"},"suggested_fix":"Add a sandbox step to smoke-remote.mjs that runs PLATFORM_ONLY's cases through POST /_worker/sandbox on a deployed Worker with CLAX_TEST_ROUTES=1, and drop each from PLATFORM_ONLY (or move it to PLATFORM_DIFFERENCES) by what it answers.","summary":"Eight conformance cases (the CPU and memory limits) have never run against LoaderSandbox: workerd enforces neither limit on a dynamic Worker","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","unverified","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:51:35.664510Z","id":"8ce7ef235190bca67b521050a103d82dbe0e8cb14af80bbda13d405e1d2c435e","body":{"detail":"The texts matched (\"exceeded CPU\", \"CPU time limit\", \"exceeded memory\", \"memory limit\") are from Cloudflare's docs for Workers and Workflows (\"Error: Worker exceeded CPU time limit.\", error 1102 \"Worker exceeded resource limits\"); the Dynamic Workers docs (developers.cloudflare.com/dynamic-workers/usage/limits/) say only that a Worker past a custom limit \"throws an exception\". workerd raises neither (record on lines 98-128). A different text makes a CPU stop end as Thrown, which the model would read as its own error, and bills nothing different.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":700},"end":{"line":749},"content_hash":"0e543d1ebe3276aa48eaa9229d0a0deaaac37c6d2731e32b4a073930ad57643c"},"suggested_fix":"Run a CPU-bound and a memory-bound script on a deployed Worker and pin the texts in tests.rs platform_failures_map_to_their_error_kinds.","summary":"platform_error tells a CPU or memory stop from other failures by the error's text, which has never been seen from a dynamic Worker","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","unverified","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/driver.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:51:35.664565Z","id":"d1e02c9471c2e0c7723b5607aa5542f52152127e11e4c50525e479c0c6306404","body":{"detail":"finish() sends the final message through `host` and then calls abortIsolate, so that no job the script queued runs after its body settles (conformance the_end_is_the_body_settling: an endless microtask loop left behind would otherwise keep the isolate from ever answering) and a call over max_calls ends the script at once (the_call_limit_cannot_be_caught). workerd 1.20261006.1 exports abortIsolate and delivered a 100 KB host call made immediately before it; the run waits FINAL_GRACE_MS (loader.rs) for that message when the aborted request's failure arrives first. If production lacks abortIsolate the driver falls back to resolving run() with the final message, and a script that leaves a microtask loop running ends with the platform's CPU limit instead of its value; if the message is not delivered before the abort, every run ends Thrown with the abort's text.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":158},"end":{"line":178},"content_hash":"02bfdc9780839bf13e59670cda85a53dc1053dfcc533c8a893795d2ac616446b"},"summary":"A script's end relies on abortIsolate from cloudflare:workers, which Cloudflare does not document, and on a host call made just before it still being delivered","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","unverified","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:51:35.664617Z","id":"ebdf6c2f9fa2cd222637ffc9f674a67240f7ddaaa6b448cdb68337939055615c","body":{"detail":"The Worker Loader reports no CPU time to the caller: a tail Worker's TraceItem.cpuTime arrives after the request, asynchronously, and was 0 under workerd. ScriptOutcome::cpu_us is therefore busy_us, the wall time (Date.now in the instance's object, advancing at each I/O) the isolate was busy between host calls, as docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md section 6.1 allows (\"else wall time\"). It overstates CPU whenever the isolate waits to be scheduled, and includes isolate start-up. mem_peak_bytes is 0 (or memory_bytes after a MemoryLimit); billing charges memory_bytes either way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":628},"end":{"line":645},"content_hash":"ae6353b1850bead1d3d62864f8da56a154ea82aa4ef1037acec57d1df6d069e2"},"suggested_fix":"Attach a tail Worker (WorkerCode.tails, a ctx.exports entrypoint in the Worker's JS shim) and reconcile the run's charge with TraceItem.cpuTime when it arrives.","summary":"The Worker sandbox bills wall time as CPU time and measures no memory","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","metering","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:51:35.664667Z","id":"832f1418aab064b3ba78d6bf7fda9d551e4661a8873fb4b11520bdda09a57cca","body":{"detail":"No WorkerCode or getEntrypoint option sets a memory limit (developers.cloudflare.com/dynamic-workers/usage/limits/ lists cpuMs and subRequests only). A script under 128 MB but over its memory_bytes runs on (PLATFORM_DIFFERENCES' the_memory_limit_ends_a_deep_structure ends ResultTooLarge, not MemoryLimit), and a memory_bytes over 128 MB is never available. Billing charges memory_bytes, as the spec asks.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":53},"content_hash":"92dfe9036ecd05a4d170776a1507336321dc0d6fc3981b1ab2c6ff0fe9b615db"},"summary":"Limits::memory_bytes bounds nothing on the Worker: every dynamic Worker has the platform's fixed 128 MB isolate limit","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/driver.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:51:35.664703Z","id":"1dd0a0aa0ee15781ed985bc101a53afb8134726c099d74141bd9d1c7292ebe4a","body":{"detail":"Under workerd 1.20261006.1, `await import('cloudflare:workers')` gave env (empty), exports, abortIsolate, RpcTarget and the entrypoint classes, and `await import('node:fs')` 106 exports. Nothing reaches outside: the isolate has globalOutbound null and no bindings, and the instance checks every host call. But conformance's no_module_loading checks only a module that does not exist, and the driver's own plumbing (RpcPromise, abortIsolate) is reachable to the script, which can only harm its own run.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":51},"end":{"line":56},"content_hash":"4b8ee30dad1d9bdcf2af06c55aa698922a61c8d58033bd5255a47db821ad518f"},"suggested_fix":"Make clax_bot_sandbox::check_body refuse import() and import.meta (an ImportExpression or MetaProperty in the body) on every sandbox, with a conformance case.","summary":"A script on the Worker can import() the runtime's built-in modules (cloudflare:workers, node:*), which QuickJS has none of","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","security","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:51:35.664744Z","id":"20bb8187d17752d572e91c05d28c1ee450c3f52a9ab1f4a11ee1c04ebf9b304c","body":{"detail":"Nothing aborts a dynamic Worker's request from the caller: the CancelToken ends the run at once and any later message from the isolate is answered with a stop (which aborts it), but a busy loop sends none. Cloudflare allows ten distinct dynamic Workers with in-flight requests per Durable Object (developers.cloudflare.com/dynamic-workers/platform/limits/); runs abandoned this way may make later loads fail, which platform_error reads as Unavailable only if the text says 'too many' or 'Failed to start Worker' (unverified). The driver (clax-bot) is to bound runs per instance below that.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":55},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"9c355cd3b07b3747c069fefe3697eaf88541efcefa4961d2cc1c3adfa9bad5c4"},"summary":"Cancelling a Worker run that never calls the host leaves its isolate running until the CPU limit ends it, and it still counts toward the object's ten concurrent dynamic Workers","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/loader.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:51:35.664794Z","id":"0612a7203963b971264492c7dc4c7e2470cf1a0804acce7148b881181ace0233","body":{"detail":"The instance passes a function of its own as run()'s second argument, which Workers RPC hands the isolate as a stub that calls back into the same object and request: the run's state stays in the run's Rust future, env stays empty, and the workers-rs shim needs no JS entrypoint class. An env binding would land each call in a fresh entrypoint request outside the object, which would have to route it back to the run by an ID.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":110},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"2df28a8309debe3781ad352a16cca24187dfe65950b80cd8be63eb2ff24e71de"},"summary":"Pass the host as a WorkerEntrypoint stub (ctx.exports with props) in the dynamic Worker's env, as docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md section 6.1 words it, instead of a function argument to run()","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","revisit:a dynamic Worker needs the host before run() is called, or Cloudflare stops passing functions over RPC","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:51:35.664837Z","id":"40d0d75a6a429906126bc8c5e845b1e3d4cf9cbad546c80b3020df347f80b1f8","body":{"detail":"ES modules are strict-mode code and reject HTML-like comments, so a module would change what scripts mean (an undeclared assignment throws, with is a syntax error) and refuse the conformance case a_first_line_may_open_with_an_html_like_comment. workerd compiles a {cjs} module as a sloppy function body: under workerd 1.20261006.1 it ran `x = 5`, `with`, octal literals, `-->` and `<!--` lines as QuickJS does, and named the module in stack traces as `<name>:<line>:<col>`, so check_body and the conformance suite stay as they are.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":323},"end":{"line":326},"content_hash":"4e8bc4a79ede8d4c0d7acd24831a5ec4c7bf342b1693b60f14fea3921359a44f"},"summary":"Load the script as an ES module and make check_body refuse HTML-like comments, rather than as CommonJS","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","revisit:Dynamic Workers stop accepting cjs modules","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:11:31.942771Z","id":"be1ca4fe4e760fbf8e5d2bef07aaf86572e35d999f757fb967b0530fe9244347","body":{"detail":"Under wrangler 4.149.0 (workerd 1.20261006.1, the newest wrangler at least two weeks old on 2026-10-21) a dynamic Worker running `for(;;){}` with `limits: {cpuMs: 100}` held the whole runtime: no request to the parent Worker was answered for 30 s, until wrangler was stopped. 5000 arrays of 10000 numbers (about 200 MB) allocated without error, past the 128 MB the platform documents. test-sandbox.mjs therefore lists PLATFORM_ONLY's cases and runs none of them; that `cpuMs` ends each of them with CpuLimit, and the 128 MB isolate limit ends the two allocation cases with MemoryLimit, is unverified until they run on a deployed Worker.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":101},"end":{"line":131},"content_hash":"2ee8e634dcf7e40aee4418080aa0857b567a85c2b7bc8448dd1e9b600ac7460a"},"suggested_fix":"Add a sandbox step to smoke-remote.mjs that runs PLATFORM_ONLY's cases through POST /_worker/sandbox on a deployed Worker with CLAX_TEST_ROUTES=1, and drop each from PLATFORM_ONLY (or move it to PLATFORM_DIFFERENCES) by what it answers.","summary":"Eight conformance cases (the CPU and memory limits) have never run against LoaderSandbox: workerd enforces neither limit on a dynamic Worker","supersedes":"1a16c82e06311cede52747c880ff16393a3a378bddc8ddb68022bfd0b5059710","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","unverified","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:11:31.963445Z","id":"e4584d2ee120fb6e6506ad00a88d221838ed25f586e0015fa157cc4f68160708","body":{"detail":"The texts matched (\"exceeded CPU\", \"CPU time limit\", \"exceeded memory\", \"memory limit\") are from Cloudflare's docs for Workers and Workflows (\"Error: Worker exceeded CPU time limit.\", error 1102 \"Worker exceeded resource limits\"); the Dynamic Workers docs (developers.cloudflare.com/dynamic-workers/usage/limits/) say only that a Worker past a custom limit \"throws an exception\". workerd raises neither (record on lines 98-128). A different text makes a CPU stop end as Thrown, which the model would read as its own error, and bills nothing different.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":760},"end":{"line":809},"content_hash":"0e543d1ebe3276aa48eaa9229d0a0deaaac37c6d2731e32b4a073930ad57643c"},"suggested_fix":"Run a CPU-bound and a memory-bound script on a deployed Worker and pin the texts in tests.rs platform_failures_map_to_their_error_kinds.","summary":"platform_error tells a CPU or memory stop from other failures by the error's text, which has never been seen from a dynamic Worker","supersedes":"8ce7ef235190bca67b521050a103d82dbe0e8cb14af80bbda13d405e1d2c435e","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","unverified","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:11:31.982210Z","id":"6dde5b5fe2b5912412c3bceb1c524ee68f7083d89517b6c2ea855beb2c8ba523","body":{"detail":"Nothing aborts a dynamic Worker's request from the caller: the CancelToken ends the run at once and any later message from the isolate is answered with a stop (which aborts it), but a busy loop sends none. Cloudflare allows ten distinct dynamic Workers with in-flight requests per Durable Object (developers.cloudflare.com/dynamic-workers/platform/limits/); runs abandoned this way may make later loads fail, which platform_error reads as Unavailable only if the text says 'too many' or 'Failed to start Worker' (unverified). The driver (clax-bot) is to bound runs per instance below that.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":58},"end":{"line":63},"content_hash":"9c355cd3b07b3747c069fefe3697eaf88541efcefa4961d2cc1c3adfa9bad5c4"},"summary":"Cancelling a Worker run that never calls the host leaves its isolate running until the CPU limit ends it, and it still counts toward the object's ten concurrent dynamic Workers","supersedes":"20bb8187d17752d572e91c05d28c1ee450c3f52a9ab1f4a11ee1c04ebf9b304c","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:11:32.000736Z","id":"94ff66eadedab7b76204cc82d677d2b0eefa6a47a9cbfcb7313a83ba3da61105","body":{"detail":"ES modules are strict-mode code and reject HTML-like comments, so a module would change what scripts mean (an undeclared assignment throws, with is a syntax error) and refuse the conformance case a_first_line_may_open_with_an_html_like_comment. workerd compiles a {cjs} module as a sloppy function body: under workerd 1.20261006.1 it ran `x = 5`, `with`, octal literals, `-->` and `<!--` lines as QuickJS does, and named the module in stack traces as `<name>:<line>:<col>`, so check_body and the conformance suite stay as they are.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":331},"end":{"line":334},"content_hash":"4e8bc4a79ede8d4c0d7acd24831a5ec4c7bf342b1693b60f14fea3921359a44f"},"summary":"Load the script as an ES module and make check_body refuse HTML-like comments, rather than as CommonJS","supersedes":"40d0d75a6a429906126bc8c5e845b1e3d4cf9cbad546c80b3020df347f80b1f8","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","revisit:Dynamic Workers stop accepting cjs modules","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/driver.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:11:32.019466Z","id":"25cc85766cae084a33554b0cf209d096a4cd98528cfb54e679c9d8ce6d578f4e","body":{"detail":"finish() sends the final message through `host` and then calls abortIsolate, so that no job the script queued runs after its body settles (conformance the_end_is_the_body_settling: an endless microtask loop left behind would otherwise keep the isolate from ever answering) and a call over max_calls ends the script at once (the_call_limit_cannot_be_caught). workerd 1.20261006.1 exports abortIsolate and delivered a 100 KB host call made immediately before it; the run waits FINAL_GRACE_MS (loader.rs) for that message when the aborted request's failure arrives first. If production lacks abortIsolate the driver falls back to resolving run() with the final message, and a script that leaves a microtask loop running ends with the platform's CPU limit instead of its value; if the message is not delivered before the abort, every run ends Thrown with the abort's text.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":166},"end":{"line":186},"content_hash":"f4967e58050ca44fb3fc00f1cb4509ebaa08230bd1fbeb2f4543ffaded027828"},"summary":"A script's end relies on abortIsolate from cloudflare:workers, which Cloudflare does not document, and on a host call made just before it still being delivered","supersedes":"d1e02c9471c2e0c7723b5607aa5542f52152127e11e4c50525e479c0c6306404","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","unverified","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:11:32.038073Z","id":"4be7925605e2fce73698c33fddadeaa7e46ef8233da4121ea4d4905f21158039","body":{"detail":"The Worker Loader reports no CPU time to the caller: a tail Worker's TraceItem.cpuTime arrives after the request, asynchronously, and was 0 under workerd 1.20261006.1. ScriptOutcome::cpu_us is therefore busy_us, the wall time (Date.now in the instance's object, advancing at each I/O) the isolate was busy between host calls, as docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md section 6.1 allows (\"else wall time\"). It overstates CPU whenever the isolate waits to be scheduled, and includes isolate start-up. Memory is not measured either: mem_peak_bytes is ISOLATE_MEMORY_BYTES (128 MiB) or memory_bytes, whichever is larger, what the script could have held.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":654},"end":{"line":668},"content_hash":"2aeb936c43b61e13652596518f5a30d74f043f0b4645e64150e6fbd7165126e3"},"suggested_fix":"Attach a tail Worker (WorkerCode.tails, a ctx.exports entrypoint in the Worker's JS shim) and reconcile the run's CPU charge with TraceItem.cpuTime when it arrives.","summary":"The Worker sandbox bills wall time as CPU time and charges memory at the isolate's limit, measuring neither","supersedes":"ebdf6c2f9fa2cd222637ffc9f674a67240f7ddaaa6b448cdb68337939055615c","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","metering","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:11:32.056690Z","id":"fa6d40c231e5c4f399e964a8146a12232139f80c1cc56a89dc53f9eb2cb9749a","body":{"detail":"No WorkerCode or getEntrypoint option sets a memory limit (developers.cloudflare.com/dynamic-workers/usage/limits/ lists cpuMs and subRequests only). A script under 128 MiB but over its memory_bytes runs on (PLATFORM_DIFFERENCES' the_memory_limit_ends_a_deep_structure ends ResultTooLarge, not MemoryLimit). Since 71ea3064 every run reports mem_peak_bytes as max(ISOLATE_MEMORY_BYTES, memory_bytes), and clax_bot_sandbox's crate docs (\"Cancellation and metering\") have billing charge the larger of that and the limit, so a Worker run is charged 128 MiB whatever memory_bytes says.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":57},"content_hash":"9d9100ea98ca055f8289be332b7e68c0b143288fcb4e0d222ed4f45cdb47258c"},"summary":"Limits::memory_bytes bounds nothing on the Worker: every dynamic Worker has the platform's fixed 128 MB isolate limit","supersedes":"832f1418aab064b3ba78d6bf7fda9d551e4661a8873fb4b11520bdda09a57cca","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/driver.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:11:32.075349Z","id":"39212ed1387fa26df8e3cf0cad4fed1ea4ac466fce6d7fe62d4e6c18055c0054","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fc43eeb6","summary":"check_body refuses import() and import.meta (fc43eeb6); conformance no_module_loading, no_loading_a_runtime_module (cloudflare:workers), no_loading_a_node_module (node:fs) and no_import_meta end with Syntax on both sandboxes: bazel test //crates/clax-bot-js:integration PASSED, test-sandbox.mjs ok for all four","supersedes":"1dd0a0aa0ee15781ed985bc101a53afb8134726c099d74141bd9d1c7292ebe4a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/loader.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:29:42.288940Z","id":"dea7545aeda5fdc98364e4bd6419d4fd9698146108fd8f714535a0e2ff697220","body":{"detail":"The instance passes a function of its own as run()'s second argument, which Workers RPC hands the isolate as a stub that calls back into the same object and request: the run's state stays in the run's Rust future, env stays empty, and the workers-rs shim needs no JS entrypoint class. An env binding would land each call in a fresh entrypoint request outside the object, which would have to route it back to the run by an ID.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":110},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"577cbfd51000ef5c2f8384d78fafb2f416080503f3168666849113bf08c8094c"},"summary":"Pass the host as a WorkerEntrypoint stub (ctx.exports with props) in the dynamic Worker's env, as docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md section 6.1 words it, instead of a function argument to run()","supersedes":"0612a7203963b971264492c7dc4c7e2470cf1a0804acce7148b881181ace0233","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","revisit:a dynamic Worker needs the host before run() is called, or Cloudflare stops passing functions over RPC","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:29:42.308993Z","id":"5ade1114e4e0fe2302556ef404ebe4f02c1350cdba937bafaf09a73012ce9843","body":{"detail":"The texts matched (\"exceeded CPU\", \"CPU time limit\", \"exceeded memory\", \"memory limit\") are from Cloudflare's docs for Workers and Workflows (\"Error: Worker exceeded CPU time limit.\", error 1102 \"Worker exceeded resource limits\"); the Dynamic Workers docs (developers.cloudflare.com/dynamic-workers/usage/limits/) say only that a Worker past a custom limit \"throws an exception\". workerd raises neither (record on lines 98-128). A different text makes a CPU stop end as Thrown, which the model would read as its own error, and bills nothing different.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":777},"end":{"line":831},"content_hash":"c961c20ffbd0b7ed3fcc58c260dc1c28b29f3d5db5f252955d10fecdf6345197"},"suggested_fix":"Run a CPU-bound and a memory-bound script on a deployed Worker and pin the texts in tests.rs platform_failures_map_to_their_error_kinds.","summary":"platform_error tells a CPU or memory stop from other failures by the error's text, which has never been seen from a dynamic Worker","supersedes":"e4584d2ee120fb6e6506ad00a88d221838ed25f586e0015fa157cc4f68160708","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","unverified","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/driver.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:29:42.333822Z","id":"a18e0b807f1c3e384d4e9029a78c411f0b053fb33913e05ccc5b8c80f4873029","body":{"detail":"finish() sends the final message through `host` and then calls abortIsolate, so that no job the script queued runs after its body settles (conformance the_end_is_the_body_settling: an endless microtask loop left behind would otherwise keep the isolate from ever answering) and a call over max_calls ends the script at once (the_call_limit_cannot_be_caught). workerd 1.20261006.1 exports abortIsolate and delivered a 100 KB host call made immediately before it; the run waits FINAL_GRACE_MS (loader.rs) for that message when the aborted request's failure arrives first. If production lacks abortIsolate the driver falls back to resolving run() with the final message, and a script that leaves a microtask loop running ends with the platform's CPU limit instead of its value; if the message is not delivered before the abort, every run ends Thrown with the abort's text.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":167},"end":{"line":187},"content_hash":"f4967e58050ca44fb3fc00f1cb4509ebaa08230bd1fbeb2f4543ffaded027828"},"summary":"A script's end relies on abortIsolate from cloudflare:workers, which Cloudflare does not document, and on a host call made just before it still being delivered","supersedes":"25cc85766cae084a33554b0cf209d096a4cd98528cfb54e679c9d8ce6d578f4e","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","unverified","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:29:42.354174Z","id":"2b0ab9a57a43b8490bd43ecf34e72b56353768d8065328e7cbb7c6af1e721665","body":{"detail":"The Worker Loader reports no CPU time to the caller: a tail Worker's TraceItem.cpuTime arrives after the request, asynchronously, and was 0 under workerd 1.20261006.1. ScriptOutcome::cpu_us is therefore busy_us, the wall time (Date.now in the instance's object, advancing at each I/O) the isolate was busy between host calls, as docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md section 6.1 allows (\"else wall time\"). It overstates CPU whenever the isolate waits to be scheduled, and includes isolate start-up. Memory is not measured either: mem_peak_bytes is ISOLATE_MEMORY_BYTES (128 MiB) or memory_bytes, whichever is larger, what the script could have held.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":672},"end":{"line":690},"content_hash":"e21bdf83121509b855fc96fc8492b80e0d0485eaeabb7a425f47b14a0919b788"},"suggested_fix":"Attach a tail Worker (WorkerCode.tails, a ctx.exports entrypoint in the Worker's JS shim) and reconcile the run's CPU charge with TraceItem.cpuTime when it arrives.","summary":"The Worker sandbox bills wall time as CPU time and charges memory at the isolate's limit, measuring neither","supersedes":"4be7925605e2fce73698c33fddadeaa7e46ef8233da4121ea4d4905f21158039","tags":["claxbot","sandbox","metering","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
